               "headline":  "Record quarter, but the Marvell deal now makes LITE trade like a falling MRVL",
               "summary":  "Lumentum fell 13.94% on 20 Nov 2026 to $460.54, about 60% below its $1,143 peak on 9 Oct. The business itself is booming: Q1 FY27 revenue rose 136.5% to $1.26B, and Q2 guidance is $1.575–1.625B. The stock, though, now trades mainly as a stand-in for Marvell. Marvell agreed on 2 Nov to buy Lumentum for 4.5 MRVL shares per LITE share, all in stock. MRVL has lost about 49% in a month. LITE also carries a discount for the risk that China delays or blocks a deal not expected to close until the first half of 2028. The chart is clearly bearish, with RSI right at the oversold line.",
