               "opportunityCheck":  "The sub-scores mostly hold up, and the latest quarter supports them. I would raise \u0027position\u0027 from 14 to about 16. Revenue more than doubled and the non-GAAP operating margin is guided at 45–46%, which takes real pricing power. Customers also signed more than $5B of purchase commitments for a second co-packaged optics program, so they are locking in Lumentum\u0027s lasers. Keep in mind the scores rate the business, not the stock. Until the Marvell deal closes or falls apart, the share price will follow MRVL and deal risk more than these fundamentals.",
               "technical":  "Trend: EMAs (exponential moving averages, trend lines that weight recent days more) all sit far above the price. At $460.54, LITE is below the EMA 50 ($755.25), EMA 100 ($796.37) and EMA 200 ($739.60), and about 38% under the 200-day. The EMA 50 has already crossed below the EMA 100 and is closing in on the EMA 200. Momentum: MACD (the gap between the 12- and 26-day EMAs) is −92.53, below its signal line at −85.66, with a histogram of −6.88. Selling momentum is still growing. RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold) is 30.07, so the stock is stretched and short bounces can happen. Volatility: the Bollinger Bands are extremely wide, from $380.78 to $929.40. Price is in the lower half of the bands, above the lower band, and in the bottom quarter of its 52-week range ($229.59–$1,143). Volume: the 20 Nov drop traded 5.76M shares, about 90% of the 20-day average. That is heavy selling but not the volume spike that usually marks capitulation (the final panic sell-off). On 20 Nov the stock opened at its high of $515.91 and sold off all day. Support sits near the lower band at about $381. Resistance is $515.91, then about $535 (the 19 Nov close).",
               "fundamental":  "Lumentum makes the indium-phosphide laser chips (EMLs and continuous-wave lasers for silicon photonics and CPO) that go into 800G and 1.6T AI transceivers. It also makes optical circuit switches (OCS). Q1 FY27, the quarter to 26 Sep reported on 2 Nov: revenue $1,262.6M (+136.5% y/y, +25.5% q/q), of which components were $754.2M and systems $508.4M. GAAP net income was $360.3M and non-GAAP EPS $4.57. Q2 guidance: revenue $1.575–1.625B, non-GAAP operating margin 45–46%, EPS $5.90–6.20. Management sees OCS becoming a multi-billion-dollar annual business. None of this weakens the tight-supply laser moat. What changed is what holders own: if the deal closes, LITE becomes about 33% of a combined Marvell, so the investment turns into a bet on Marvell with Lumentum inside.",
               "news":  [
                            "2 Nov 2026: Q1 FY27 revenue was $1,262.6M (+136.5% y/y), GAAP EPS $3.54 and non-GAAP EPS $4.57. Q2 guidance of $1.575–1.625B came alongside a second CPO win backed by more than $5B of purchase commitments.",
                            "2 Nov 2026: Marvell agreed to buy Lumentum in an all-stock deal at 4.5 MRVL shares per LITE share, an implied $115B enterprise value, expected to close in the first half of 2028. LITE fell 18.6% and MRVL 12.7% that day.",
                            "3 Nov 2026: TD Cowen cut its target to $685 from $820 (Hold), and Susquehanna cut to $950 from $1,100 (Positive). Both tied the cuts to the fixed exchange ratio.",
